## 2. Scale-search objective (packing._w4_search scores 16 candidates by squared WEIGHT error)
== L1.kda.in_proj  (6416, 4096)
   A. scale-search objective                 RTN  GPTQ act_order
      identity                      3.6035e-02      2.2193e-02   (+0% / +0%) [ships]
      diag                          3.5828e-02      2.2303e-02   (-1% / +0%)
      block                         3.4579e-02      2.2553e-02   (-4% / +2%)
== L1.kda.o_proj  (4096, 2048)
      identity                      7.4753e-02      4.9114e-02   (+0% / +0%) [ships]
      diag                          6.8370e-02      4.9484e-02   (-9% / +1%)
      block                         6.5093e-02      5.0114e-02   (-13% / +2%)
# Helps RTN, costs 2% under GPTQ: the two are substitutes and GPTQ is the stronger one.

## 3. Can damping or shrinkage patch a stale Hessian?  (GPTQ act_order, block-weighted scales)
== in_proj   ceiling (matched calibration)   2.2553e-02
      rh-era, percdamp=0.01                  3.9680e-02
      rh-era, percdamp=0.05                  3.9783e-02
      rh-era, percdamp=0.20                  3.9795e-02
      rh-era, shrink=0.25                    3.9971e-02
      rh-era, shrink=0.50                    4.0121e-02
== o_proj   ceiling (matched calibration)    5.0114e-02
      rh-era, percdamp=0.01                  8.9496e-02
      rh-era, percdamp=0.05                  8.7148e-02
      rh-era, percdamp=0.20                  8.6367e-02
      rh-era, shrink=0.25                    8.7860e-02
      rh-era, shrink=0.50                    8.6767e-02
# No. o_proj recovers ~10% of the gap, in_proj none.

## 4. So what IS the best pack a node with only a stale Hessian can build?
== L1.kda.in_proj   everything below is built from the STALE rh-era Hessian only
      RTN, identity scales (no Hessian at all)   3.6035e-02   <- wins
      RTN, stale-weighted scales                 4.5173e-02
      GPTQ act_order, stale                      3.9680e-02
== L1.kda.o_proj
      RTN, identity scales (no Hessian at all)   7.4753e-02   <- wins
      RTN, stale-weighted scales                 8.5846e-02
      GPTQ act_order, stale                      8.9496e-02
# A stale Hessian is worth less than no Hessian, every way of using it.

